.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd November 20, 2026
.Dt NOQTIS-SMIME 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm noqtis-smime
.Nd sign, verify, encrypt or decrypt mail (S/MIME, CMS)
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm noqtis smime
.Cm sign
.Fl k Ar key
.Fl -cert Ar cert
.Op Fl -detached
.Op Fl -der
.Op Fl -text | Fl -entity
.Op Fl o Ar out
.Op Fl -force
.Op Fl -pass-fd Ar n | Fl -pass-env Ar name
.Ar file
.Nm noqtis smime
.Cm verify
.Fl -anchor Ar cert
.Op Fl -anchor Ar cert ...
.Op Fl -content Ar file
.Op Fl -entity
.Op Fl o Ar out
.Op Fl -force
.Ar file
.Nm noqtis smime
.Cm encrypt
.Fl -to Ar cert
.Op Fl -to Ar cert ...
.Op Fl -der
.Op Fl -text | Fl -entity
.Op Fl o Ar out
.Op Fl -force
.Ar file
.Nm noqtis smime
.Cm decrypt
.Fl k Ar key
.Op Fl -cert Ar cert
.Op Fl -entity
.Op Fl o Ar out
.Op Fl -force
.Op Fl -pass-fd Ar n | Fl -pass-env Ar name
.Ar file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm noqtis smime
writes and reads S/MIME messages (RFC 8551), the signed and encrypted
mail of the Cryptographic Message Syntax (RFC 5652), with the
certificates
.Xr noqtis-cert 1
makes.
.Bl -tag -width "encrypt"
.It Cm sign
Sign
.Ar file
with the secret signature key
.Ar key ,
whose certificate is
.Fl -cert Ar cert :
ML-DSA (RFC 9882), SLH-DSA (RFC 9814) or Ed25519 (RFC 8419).
The message carries the certificate.
With
.Fl -detached
the content stays in the clear beside the signature
.Pq multipart/signed ,
so that a reader without S/MIME still shows it; otherwise it is inside
.Pq application/pkcs7-mime .
.It Cm verify
Check a signed message against the trust anchors given with
.Fl -anchor
(up to 32 certificates, PEM or DER): the signer's certificate is one of
them, or chains to one.
It prints who signed, and with
.Fl o
writes the content.
The certificates must be valid at the signing time the message states.
.It Cm encrypt
Encrypt
.Ar file
to the ML-KEM certificates given with
.Fl -to
(up to 32): AES-256-GCM, the content key carried to each recipient by
ML-KEM (RFC 9629, RFC 9936).
Encryption does not say who sent a message: to do both, sign first and
encrypt the result.
.It Cm decrypt
Open an encrypted message with the ML-KEM secret key
.Ar key ;
.Fl -cert
names that key's certificate, and so its entry among the recipients.
.El
.Pp
The options:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -der
Write the CMS structure itself, in DER, in place of a MIME message.
.Cm verify
and
.Cm decrypt
read either form;
.Cm verify
takes what a detached DER signature signs with
.Fl -content Ar file .
.It Fl -text
The content is text: it is carried as it is
.Pq text/plain ,
readable in a detached message, and its line ends become CRLF as S/MIME
requires.
Without it the content is carried in base64 and every byte comes back
as it was.
.It Fl -entity
.Ar file
is a MIME entity already, header and body;
.Cm verify
and
.Cm decrypt
then write the entity instead of its body.
.It Fl o Ar out , Fl -out Ns = Ns Ar out
The output; standard output when it is not given or is
.Ar - .
.It Fl -pass-fd Ar n , Fl -pass-env Ar name
The passphrase of a protected
.Ar key .
.It Fl f , Fl -force
Replace an existing
.Ar out .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success;
1 when
.Cm verify
finds that a signature does not verify or its signer is not trusted;
2 on a usage or file error, and when a message does not open.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal
$ noqtis smime sign -k me --cert me.crt --detached --text \e
      -o note.eml note.txt
$ noqtis smime verify --anchor me.crt note.eml
note.eml: OK, signed by Ada Example <ada@example.org> (certificate ...)
$ noqtis smime encrypt --to bob-kem.crt -o secret.p7m report.pdf
$ noqtis smime decrypt -k bob-kem -o report.pdf secret.p7m
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-cert 1 ,
.Xr nqcmssign 3 ,
.Xr nqsmsign 3
.Sh STANDARDS
.Rs
.%A J. Schaad
.%A B. Ramsdell
.%A S. Turner
.%T Secure/Multipurpose Internet Mail Extensions (S/MIME) Version 4.0 Message Specification
.%R RFC 8551
.%D April 2019
.Re
